B.Vf=new A.ed("frightened","PHB","A frightened creature has disadvantage on ability checks and attack rolls while the source of its fear is within line of sight. The creature can't willingly move closer to the source of its fear.",B.w5,B.bo)
B.a6K=new A.bi(B.a8q,[B.Vf],t.v)
B.a8x={mirrorImage:0}
B.UX=new A.ed("mirrorImage","PHB","While this condition is active, each time a creature targets the caster with an attack, the caster must roll a d20 to determine whether the attack instead targets one of the caster\u2019s duplicates.\n\n- If the caster has three duplicates, a roll of 6 or higher causes the attack to target a duplicate.\n- If the caster has two duplicates, a roll of 8 or higher is required.\n- If the caster has one duplicate, a roll of 11 or higher is required.\n\nEach duplicate has an Armor Class equal to 10 + the caster\u2019s Dexterity modifier. If an attack hits a duplicate, that duplicate is destroyed.\n\nA duplicate can only be destroyed by an attack that successfully hits it. Duplicates are unaffected by all other damage and effects.\n\nThis condition ends when all duplicates are destroyed.",B.ow,B.ca)
B.a7n=new A.bi(B.a8x,[B.UX],t.v)
B.a8v={invisible:0}
B.vQ=new A.ck("Invisible","assets/icons/invisible.svg",B.dj,25,"invisible")
B.Vd=new A.ed("invisible","PHB","An invisible creature is impossible to see without the aid of magic or a special sense. For the purpose of hiding, the creature is heavily obscured. The creature's location can be detected by any noise it makes or any tracks it leaves. Attack rolls against the creature have disadvantage, and the creature's attack rolls have advantage.",B.vQ,B.bo)
B.a6G=new A.bi(B.a8v,[B.Vd],t.v)
B.a8B={petrified:0}
B.vX=new A.ck("Petrified","assets/icons/petrified.svg",B.dj,26,"petrified")
B.V7=new A.ed("petrified","PHB","A petrified creature is transformed, along with any nonmagical object it is wearing or carrying, into a solid inanimate substance (usually stone). Its weight increases by a factor of ten, and it ceases aging. The creature is incapacitated, can't move or speak, and is unaware of its surroundings. Attack rolls against the creature have advantage. The creature automatically fails Strength and Dexterity saving throws. The creature has resistance to all damage. The creature is immune to poison and disease, although a poison or disease already in its system is suspended, not neutralized.",B.vX,B.ca)
B.a7D=new A.bi(B.a8B,[B.V7],t.v)
B.a8G={reactionUsed:0}
B.vR=new A.ck("Reaction Used","assets/icons/ReactionUsed.svg",B.dj,27,"reactionUsed")
B.V9=new A.ed("reactionUsed","PHB","When a creature's reaction has been used, it can no longer take another reaction until the start of its next turn. This means the creature cannot make opportunity attacks, use spells like Counterspell or Shield, or respond to other triggers requiring a reaction until it regains its ability to do so.",B.vR,B.od)
B.a7c=new A.bi(B.a8G,[B.V9],t.v)
